# Shared clang-tidy baseline for tlv (C) and tlv++ (C++), run by the opt-in
# 'clang-tidy' CMake target (cmake/clang_tidy.cmake) and the Static Analysis
# CI job (.github/workflows/static-analysis.yml). src/.clang-tidy disables
# C++ checks for C implementations. The former tlv++ profile is retained as
# cmake/clang-tidy-cxx.yaml for explicit --config-file use; the CMake test-TU
# analysis keeps its existing root configuration selection.
#
# clang-diagnostic-*/clang-analyzer-* surface compiler warnings and the
# Clang Static Analyzer's semantic bug-finding; bugprone-*/performance-*/
# portability-*/readability-* mirror the categories the 'cppcheck' target
# already enables (see cmake/cppcheck.cmake), for consistency between the
# two tools. The exclusions below are checks that are either pure style
# preferences conflicting with this codebase's established conventions, or
# that would require broad, correctness-unrelated rewrites to satisfy:
#
# - readability-braces-around-statements: conflicts with the project's
#   deliberate `if (cond) return x;` style (AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingle
#   Line in .clang-format).
# - readability-magic-numbers: this is a binary-protocol library; bit widths,
#   shift amounts and wire-format limits are inherent to the domain, not
#   unnamed constants that need extracting.
# - readability-identifier-length: short, idiomatic names (i, rc, a, b) are
#   established style throughout tlv/tlv++.
# - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: several parser/codec
#   functions are inherently branchy; splitting them up is a larger,
#   separate refactor, not a static-analysis fix.
# - readability-isolate-declaration: multi-variable declarations are used
#   throughout and are not a readability problem in this codebase.
# - readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator: short 3-way ternary
#   chains are a common, readable idiom here (e.g. ASN.1 length-size
#   classification); rewriting them as if/else is a style preference, not a
#   correctness fix.
# - readability-math-missing-parentheses: fires pervasively on well-known,
#   already-correct bit-shift/BCD arithmetic (e.g. src/core/endian.c); adding
#   parentheses everywhere would be pure churn.
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: extremely noisy for a byte-buffer
#   API built on (data, size) parameter pairs; not a real defect signal here.
# - clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding: an opt-in, performance-only
#   suggestion to reorder public struct fields for cache-line padding;
#   reordering public API struct layout for a marginal size saving is out of
#   scope and unrelated to correctness.
Checks: >
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
